            "text": "{\"title\":\"Make-Ahead Citrus and Achiote Braised Pork Roast\",\"readyInMinutes\":240,\"servings\":8,\"summary\":\"This flavorful \u003cb\u003emake-ahead Mexican spiced pork roast\u003c/b\u003e offers a deeply savory profile infused with traditional citrus and citrus-achiote marinades. Prepared by marinating a tender pork shoulder in a rich blend of toasted guajillo chiles, freshly squeezed orange juice, garlic, and aromatic spices, this recipe allows the bold flavors to penetrate deeply into the meat long before it touches the oven. Because the centerpiece of this dish relies on slow roasting in a tightly covered Dutch oven, it develops a melt-in-your-mouth tenderness that actually improves after resting overnight in its concentrated braising juices. Perfect for entertaining, home cooks can complete the full braising process a day early, cool the roast, and simply reheat it slowly before serving to yield an even richer texture and balanced spice. Serve this tender shredded pork alongside warm corn tortillas, pickled red onions, fresh cilantro, and soft black beans for a festive dinner feast. This \u003cb\u003eslow-braised pork roast\u003c/b\u003e simplifies party prep while delivering authentic vibrant Mexican culinary tradition straight to your home dining table.\",\"nutrition\":{\"nutrients\":[{\"name\":\"Calories\",\"amount\":520,\"unit\":\"kcal\",\"percentOfDailyNeeds\":26},{\"name\":\"Fat\",\"amount\":34,\"unit\":\"g\",\"percentOfDailyNeeds\":52},{\"name\":\"Saturated Fat\",\"amount\":12,\"unit\":\"g\",\"percentOfDailyNeeds\":60},{\"name\":\"Carbohydrates\",\"amount\":8,\"unit\":\"g\",\"percentOfDailyNeeds\":3},{\"name\":\"Sugar\",\"amount\":4,\"unit\":\"g\",\"percentOfDailyNeeds\":4},{\"name\":\"Protein\",\"amount\":44,\"unit\":\"g\",\"percentOfDailyNeeds\":88},{\"name\":\"Cholesterol\",\"amount\":140,\"unit\":\"mg\",\"percentOfDailyNeeds\":47},{\"name\":\"Sodium\",\"amount\":850,\"unit\":\"mg\",\"percentOfDailyNeeds\":37},{\"name\":\"Fi